00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.710
Let's start with a quick refresher

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.260
on John Cena's Peacemaker.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.700
The character, who made his
on-screen debut last year

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.350
in Gunn's "The Suicide Squad,"

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.090
has a pretty straightforward ethos.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.150
- I cherish peace with all my heart.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.080
I don't care how many men, women,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.460
and children I need to kill to get it.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.740
- [Michael] And by the end of the film,

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.090
it was clear that, for him,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.930
fighting for peace means
murdering your own comrades

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.360
to cover up the violent secrets

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.410
of your government's dirty
deeds, among other things.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.440
It was clear that Gunn
was using the character

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.430
to comment on both the murderous exploits

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.880
of our favorite superheroes

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.960
and the logic they use to justify

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.290
their astronomical body counts.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.950
Peacemaker isn't the
first modern superhero

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.180
to ponder whether or not it can be ethical

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.210
to commit violence,

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.820
and violate human rights in
the name of the greater good.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.837
- What if we aren't as safe?

00:03:00.837 --> 00:03:03.340
- But if next time, aliens
roll up to the club,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.630
and they will, they couldn't
get past the bouncer?

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.370
- But to really understand the history

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.320
of good guys doing violence,

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:12.030
we have to go all the way
back to St. Augustine.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.670
No, not the historic Florida city

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.520
where I took field trips in high school,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.910
the theologian and church
father who is credited

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.860
with inventing Just War Theory.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.760
This is the idea that,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.460
because God gives governments
power for good reason,

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.440
it can be ethical for those governments

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.180
to wage war under certain conditions.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.030
And this theory has helped many
a nation justify many a war.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.350
According to this theory,

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.060
the criteria for a Just War includes:

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.610
Last Resort, force can only be used

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.020
after all peaceful options
have been exhausted;

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.720
Legitimate Authority, i.e.,

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.380
a just war can only be
pursued by a government;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.240
Just Cause, war needs to be
in response to some wrong,

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.440
or attack, suffered;

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.090
Probability of Success,

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.200
there needs to be a rational
possibility of winning;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.540
Right Intention, the aim of war needs

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.360
to be the re-establishment of peace;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.590
Proportionality, the
violence inflicted needs

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.620
to be proportional to violence suffered;

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.330
and Civilian Casualties,

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.380
innocent victims should
never be the target of war,

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.300
and soldiers should avoid harming them.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.800
Now, if we were to use
Augustine's criteria

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.150
to evaluate the antics
of Peacemaker and Co.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.650
in "The Suicide Squad" film,

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.390
it doesn't seem like they're
waging a pure and holy war.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:23.390
For one, they violate the
Last Resort criterion,

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:24.880
using violence first,

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.620
rather than exhausting all other options.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.450
Then again, you probably
don't want Harley Quinn

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.270
engaging in diplomacy.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.430
What's more, it arguably fails

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.990
on the legitimate authority front.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.170
Peacemaker's actions don't seem to be tied

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.570
to a legitimate government authority,

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:44.640
as Task Force X functions more
as a sketchy black ops squad

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.060
rather than, say, the
Department of Defense.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.530
And of course, there's no
proportionality happening,

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.080
as Peacemaker seems unlimited
in his violent potential,

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.050
even when it comes to his coworkers.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.410
I guess this is what happens

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.570
when you don't have an HR department.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.540
And throughout the film,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.240
we never get any
indication he is concerned

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.890
about his actions being
anything less than just.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.210
But in the new series,

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.040
Peacemaker seems more doubtful
about his own motives,

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.470
and is openly haunted by
memories of killing Rick Flag.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.460
Right off the bat,

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.930
we see Peacemaker being
grilled by a janitor

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.021
about his suspicious killing tendencies.

00:05:21.021 --> 00:05:22.670
- Oh, Peacemaker!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.503
- Yes.

00:05:23.503 --> 00:05:25.323
- You're that racist superhero.

00:05:25.323 --> 00:05:26.156
- No.

00:05:26.156 --> 00:05:27.330
- You only care about minorities, man.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.250
- Later in the series,

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.950
he finds himself unable
to pull the trigger

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.620
when tasked with
assassinating a whole family,

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.410
including their two children.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.530
- Peacemaker, take 'em out.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.363
- Even kids?

00:05:37.363 --> 00:05:38.196
- [Man] Yes.

00:05:38.196 --> 00:05:39.440
- Mind you, these children are possessed

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.920
by alien butterflies,

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.600
but shooting a kid is still a, still bad,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.910
it's just a bad vibe.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.400
Here, Peacemaker struggles
with some Just War criteria,

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.080
including civilian casualties

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.020
and having the right intentions.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.330
Soon after, rather than killing the leader

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.790
of the butterflies,
Peacemaker keeps him in a jar,

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.620
and feeds him alien goo.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.500
But it's much less fashionable these days,

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.210
as questions of war have
now largely transitioned

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.810
into matters of national security.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.460
The current theory used
in international relations

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.300
to understand how states justify violence

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.500
is called Securitization,
or, Security Theory.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.110
Now, the Just War method
of evaluating the goodness

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.610
of bombs and bullets was all the rage

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.640
in the first part of the 20th century,

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.460
as Democratic nations were responding

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.760
to large-scale fascism and genocide,

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.020
but it's much less fashionable these days,

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.620
as questions of war have
now largely transitioned

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.840
into matters of national security.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.210
The current theory used
international relations

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.730
to understand how states justify violence

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.710
is called securitization,
or security theory.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.960
Now, the Just War Theory
sought to understand

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.010
what responses a government could take

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.240
after they were already
under some type of attack.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.520
In contrast, securitization is all

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.630
about the national security
measures a state can justify

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.960
based on potential future threats,

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.440
ostensibly to keep its people safe.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.910
It's like if there are reports

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.760
that another nation is
developing some new type

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.270
of high-powered weapons.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.080
Under securitization,
even if these weapons

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.570
haven't been employed yet,

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.030
states might use the
specter of these threats

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.970
to justify preemptive countermeasures.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.050
In this way of thinking,

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.320
the response is to what might happen,

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.530
rather than to what

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.440
has happened.
(gunshots firing)

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.890
Like how America invaded Iraq based

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.440
on speculative threat,
(airplanes zooming)

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.350
rather than in response
to an actual attack.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:29.210
Or how the speculative threat
of future terrorism led

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.150
to the passing of the Patriot Act,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.930
which many argue violates
individual liberties

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.470
and freedoms in the name of security.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.494
For scholar Mark Neocleous,

00:07:38.494 --> 00:07:40.980
the "logic of security
lies not in a vision

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.500
of freedom and emancipation,

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.540
but in a means of modeling the whole

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.370
of human society around a
particular vision or order."

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.540
Under the traditional Just War model,

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:53.840
violence was only necessary to
protect a state from attack.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.540
But under securitization,

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:58.290
states can arguably use perceived threats

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.000
to create systems of order.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.500
This can lead to citizens being forced

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.880
to surrender themselves
to the will of the state

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.550
under the guise of
protection and security.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.220
Measures like these can make the line

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.010
between right and wrong a little murky.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.330
And this seems to be at the heart

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.310
of Peacemaker's original ethos,

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.150
as a number of militaristic
sins can be forgiven

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:19.110
under the guise of security,

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.380
i.e. preventing potential threats,

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.210
which becomes another way of saying peace.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.380
Including things like murdering civilians

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.530
who just happened to be in the wrong place

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:29.690
at the wrong time.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.410
But for Mark Neocleous,

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.720
often the security offered is just a way

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.947
to conveniently suspend the law:

00:08:35.947 --> 00:08:38.990
"The idea that the permanent
emergency involves a suspension

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.090
of the law encourages the idea

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.590
that resistance must involve
a return to legality,

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.900
a return to the normal mode of governing

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.310
through the rule of law.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.570
This involves a serious misjudgment

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.300
in which it is simply assumed
that legal procedures,

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.170
both international and domestic,

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.670
are designed to protect human
rights from state violence."

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.310
According to Mark Neocleous,

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.150
the effect of securitization
is often creating a type

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.420
of permanent emergency that
suspends the law momentarily,

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.253
with the promise that

00:09:08.253 --> 00:09:10.020
this temporary suspension
(siren wailing)

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.040
will help us get back to the normal mode

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.910
of governing through the rule of law.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.540
But according to his critique,

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.870
this involves a serious
misjudgment in which we assume

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.390
that the law is designed
to protect our rights

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.940
and freedoms in the first place,

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:25.700
rather than simply to
give the state more power.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:29.400
The idea here is that if the
end goal is a return to normal,

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.233
and in particular,

00:09:30.233 --> 00:09:31.690
a peaceful normal,
(gunshots firing)

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.890
then violence can be easily justified.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.990
And this logic seems to
be one that Peacemaker,

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:37.740
and other members of his team,

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:40.070
are wrestling with throughout the series.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.290
We see this logic of securitization
in "The Suicide Squad"

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.600
when the team is initially
under the impression

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.960
that their mission is for the sake

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:50.230
of taking down some bad guys,
and one giant alien monster,

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.847
who could potentially
kill a bunch of people.

00:09:52.847 --> 00:09:56.780
(dramatic music)
(people groaning)

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:57.710
(monster thuds)

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:59.310
But it's later revealed

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:00.990
that they are simply covering the tracks

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.590
of the US government, who
are behind the whole thing,

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:04.460
to begin with.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.790
- Child, your government
didn't send you here

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.770
to protect the world
from alien technology.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:14.520
Your government sent you here
to cover up their part in it.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.070
- And while this reveal
eventually turns most

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.730
of the team against the government

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.520
for the sake of protecting human life,

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:23.170
Peacemaker doubles down, as for him,

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:26.420
protecting American secrets
and preserving peace

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.090
are one and the same.

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.930
And the series has a
similar vibe early on,

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.770
as the team's mission is motivated

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.700
by the same logic of security,

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.390
even when they're largely left in the dark

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:39.060
about why they are actually
taking out the butterflies.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.770
Which, again, are alien butterflies

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:42.500
that embed themselves in human brains

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.190
to control their bodies.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.127
But the simple logic remains:

00:10:46.127 --> 00:10:47.270
(gunshot fires)
These butterflies are

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.840
a speculative threat to national security,

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:52.450
and must be taken out at all costs.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.790
Even if that means some
collateral kills along the way.

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:58.900
Of course, this gets complicated
as the team learns more

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.040
about who they are actually fighting.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.810
They eventually learn that the butterflies

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:06.050
are also motivated by the
logic of securitization.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:06.960
The only difference

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.150
is that theirs skews more
toward environmentalism

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.140
than militarism or nationalism.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.120
And this type of
climate-based securitization

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.080
is increasingly becoming a real thing

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.640
in places like the EU.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.080
After losing their home planet

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.210
to a gradually destroyed ecosystem,

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.290
the butterflies are attempting
to help humans avoid

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.700
the same fate by covertly taking over

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.730
the political system

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:29.110
to prioritize climate protection efforts.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.020
- The people people of Earth were

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.520
on the exact same trajectory
as our people have been,

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.990
ignoring science in
favor of populist leaders

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.570
who tell you that the floods and the fires

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:39.810
and the disease are unrelated
to your own actions.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.530
- [Michael] However, in order to do this,

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.130
they need to take over the bodies

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.590
of otherwise innocent human beings,

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:47.770
effectively killing them in the process.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:48.810
The butterflies, then,

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.670
beg the same question that
Peacemaker's actions do:

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.610
Can you justify killing people

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.120
in order to preserve the
peace and greater good?

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.340
But Peacemaker and Co.
appear to be motivated

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:01.140
to stop the butterflies based on the intel

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:03.910
that the butterflies are
attempting to take over the planet,

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.400
and must be stopped at all
costs to protect humanity.

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:10.300
And here, the government is using a threat

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.820
to justify extreme security measures.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:15.740
Ironically, of course,
that threat is an attempt

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.710
to save the earth from
environmental catastrophe.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.720
- We made a vow to make
the choices for you

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.120
that you were incapable
of making on your own,

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.100
to save your people, and your world.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.820
- [Michael] Now, the
Peacemaker of The Suicide Squad

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.970
would seemingly have no problem

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.580
with eradicating the butterflies

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.790
out of a militant commitment to the ideals

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.240
of the security state.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.410
This version of the character

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.470
is just a raw embodiment of that logic.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.950
At its most extreme,

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.280
it seems that with this
version of the character,

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.330
Gunn is exploring the
dark side of America's Id.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:48.650
He even goes so far

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:52.350
as to make Peacemaker's
dad a literal Nazi.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:55.690
- All hail the White Dragon.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:56.650
- But don't worry,

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.330
Peacemaker kills him.
(gunshot fires)

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.050
Make of that what you will.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.980
So, does Peacemaker offer
any type of solution

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:05.740
for the problems inherent
in modern securitization?

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.800
In one sense,

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.470
the show and its titular character

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.350
pretty explicitly question
and criticize the type

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.660
of security measures used by
contemporary Western nations.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.880
Whether it's Adebayo
struggling to understand

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.950
how it's necessary to casually
kill innocent bystanders,

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:23.040
or Peacemaker being unable
to take out children

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.270
as part of a mission,

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.150
the team is openly
grappling with their loyalty

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:28.340
to the security state.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.640
But by the end of the season,

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:32.580
the show has taken an
almost fatalistic approach

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.470
to the idea of morally justified violence.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:37.460
The whole team has become disillusioned

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.040
by Amanda Waller and Taskforce X,

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.890
with Adebayo going so far as to snitch

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:44.820
on her own mother on TV.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.570
- It's been running for years
out of Belle Reve Prison,

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:53.700
under the command of a
woman named Amanda Waller.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.390
- Seemingly a critique of securitization.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:58.440
The show also seems to cast some doubt

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.500
on the morality of the good
type of securitization endorsed

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.550
by the butterflies,

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.340
in which rights can be curtailed

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.570
and violence can be imposed for the sake

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.980
of saving the planet, and
thus humanity as a whole.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:13.130
Ultimately, Peacemaker stops
the remaining butterflies

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:14.460
from carrying out their plan.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.822
- Activate Human Torpedo.

00:14:15.822 --> 00:14:16.655
(air whooshes)

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:17.681
- [Woman] What?

00:14:17.681 --> 00:14:20.649
(woman screaming)

00:14:20.649 --> 00:14:21.510
(creature roars)

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.870
- Not out of disagreement with
their ideological position,

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.820
one he seems to agree with,

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.740
and later regrets interfering with.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.573
- Did I just

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:32.473
kill the woman?

00:14:32.473 --> 00:14:36.630
- [Michael] Rather, he does so
simply because enabling them

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:39.030
might have led to his
friends being killed.

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.590
- Why did you choose not to help them?

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.420
- 'Cause I knew they'd hurt
you and the others if I did.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:45.640
- And now that he's killed his Nazi dad,

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.000
and he's seemingly moved
beyond his old commitment

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.330
to American security,

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:52.710
it seems like friendship is
all he has left to believe in.

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:55.300
At the end of the day, the
show seems to be saying,

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:58.080
the logic of securitization is so rampant

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.530
that we're probably screwed either way,

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:03.620
so in the meantime, maybe
look out for your friends,

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.720
take the time to rock out on long drives,

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:08.220
and try to avoid being a literal Nazi.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.200
And in doing so,

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.230
the show is also pretty transgressive

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.840
in the context of recent
DCEU and MCU content.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.170
It's forcing us to ask if maybe some

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.850
of our heroes are actually the bad guys,

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.280
and if the logic used
to justify their actions

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:24.950
is eerily similar to the political logic

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.660
of our own societies.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.010
But what do you guys think?

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.650
Is Peacemaker a hilarious

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.760
and violent critique of securitization?

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.700
Or, are we just trying to justify rooting

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.590
for such an odious character?

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.440
Let us know what you
think in the comments.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.810
Thanks to all of our amazing patrons,

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.970
and don't forget to
check out our podcasts.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:44.420
Hit that Subscribe button like
you're a Peacemaker helmet

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.760
in Human Torpedo mode,

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:47.410
and don't forget to ring that bell.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.951
And as always, thanks for watching. Later.

00:15:49.951 --> 00:15:52.618
(upbeat music)

